# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-12: after #1616 was opened,
trueqbit asked whether get_table_column_fields should be renamed
collect_table_column_fields.

# Decided
- trueqbit: get_table_column_fields keeps its name.
- Rejected: collect_table_column_fields - collect_ in this tree names the
  serializer's collectors (collect_table_names, collect_column_expressions,
  collect_table_column_expressions, collect_cte_column_names), which walk
  an expression or table with a context and append to a run-time
  container; get_table_column_fields walks nothing and appends nothing -
  it filters one table definition's elements to its columns at compile
  time and returns their member pointers as a tuple, and "collect" would
  read as a sibling of collect_table_column_expressions.
- Rejected: column_fields_of - _of names a type computed from a node
  (naming convention), not a run-time value.
- get_ stays in line with its one consumer, get_column_references_of,
  which returns get_column_references(...) or get_table_column_fields(...)
  from the same branches.
